// FF9CustomMap/StreamingAssets/Data/SpecialEffects/ef091/PlayerSequence.seq
// RUNG 8 -- NIMBRA, the composed epic. 100% hand-authored; no donor, no LoadSFX of any stock id, no
// native ef###.bytes anywhere in the chain. Binding contract: rung8-epic/STORYBOARD.md (Appendix A +
// section 11, THE RETIME 2026-07-24).
//
// Clock: BattleTPS=15 -> 1 tick = 1/15 s. Total ~140 ticks ~= 9.3 s.
//   THE RETIME (STORYBOARD 11, census/DURATION-CENSUS.md candidate A "THE WHISPER"): the first cast
//   read as laggy not because 29.3 s is a long FULL cinematic (it is the stock median) but because
//   NIMBRA has no SHORT variant, so it pays that runtime on EVERY cast where a stock summon rolls
//   short ~90% of the time (btl_cmd.cs:1600). Measured against what a player actually watches per
//   cast, stock runs 5.2-14.4 s (median 9.0). This cast is 9.3 s.
//   The cut is a RE-COMPOSITION, not a squeeze: the ~9.3 s near-static blackout front-load (P0's 45-tick
//   ramp + P1's 95-tick hold = the R17 dread beat the playtest flagged) is GONE -- the pall, the wisps
//   and the whisper swell now roll in DURING a 10-tick dim instead of after a 45-tick one, and P1 no
//   longer exists as its own beat. Nothing that carries a LAW was shortened: P4 still spends its
//   law-bound 50 ticks (18 relight + 12 settle + EffectPoint + 12 + EffectPoint + 8).
//
// THE PHASE-LOCK RULE (STORYBOARD 3): after PlaySFX every wait is a fixed `Wait` -- never a clip-bound
// WaitAnimation/WaitMove/WaitTurn. The ONE clip-bound wait sits before PlaySFX, where its slack shifts
// everything uniformly and never touches the two-clock alignment.
//
// THE TWO CLOCKS, retimed together (STORYBOARD 11.2):
//   PlaySFX fires at t = 25  ->  manifest frame 0 = t 25, window Start=0 / End=110  ->  the instance
//   drains at t = 135, which is the tick WaitSFXDone below is authored to resolve on. The playlist is
//   emerge (15) | driftlook (25) | strike (30) | drift (75) = 145 ticks over a 110-tick window, EVERY
//   ENTRY AT SPEED 1 -- THE SPEED-DIVISOR DEFECT (STORYBOARD 11.9): SFXDataMesh.cs:869 divides a
//   clip-frame index by a tick count, so any Speed > 1 runs its clip out early and freezes the rig for
//   the remainder of the entry. Clips are sized to their beats instead; the boundaries are unchanged.
//   The `strike` clip opens 18 ticks before the blow (manifest frame 40, t 65) so that its LUNGE PEAK
//   -- the drive envelope's authored frame 36/59, which on the 30-frame clip shows 18 ticks in -- lands
//   on t 83, the exact tick the sting, the rift-flash and the relight fire. The shipped build put the
//   flash on the strike clip's frame 0, i.e. on the WIND-BACK; the wind-back now reads as the tension
//   before the blow, which is what STORYBOARD 3.1 P4's prose ("the arms draw back ... both points drive
//   forward ... the light returning IS the impact") always described.
//
// Every op here is on the OUR-OPS executor-derived whitelist (summons/seqlint.py); `Reflect` is the
// universal per-op gate read at UnifiedBattleSequencer.cs:191, legal on any op.
// PlayCamera and ShiftWorld appear NOWHERE, by proof, not by taste (STORYBOARD 2):
//   * PlayCamera `break`s at Configuration.Battle.Speed >= 3 in PHASE_NORMAL (UnifiedBattleSequencer.cs:
//     828-829) and the live Memoria.ini is [Battle] Speed = 5 -- a hard no-op on this install.
//   * ShiftWorld moves only battlebg.btlRoot (the actors are NOT parented to it, battlebg.cs:411-424)
//     and has no automatic restore (UnshiftWorld has zero callers).
// The linter REFUSES both ops outright with those citations.

// ---- P0  THE HUSH + THE GATHER  (t 0 -> 25)  [P1 IS FOLDED IN HERE -- THE OVERLAP] ----------------
// The title plate, the chant, the summon aura, the drone, a FAST slide to black (Time=10, not 45), and
// -- on the same tick, not after the dim -- the floor pall, the wisps and the whisper swell. The dread
// beat is now carried by the mist arriving THROUGH the darkening instead of by six seconds of holding
// on an empty black screen.
WaitAnimation: Char=Caster
Message: Text=[CastName] ; Priority=1 ; Title=True ; Reflect=True
SetupReflect: Delay=SFXLoaded
LoadSFX: SFX=91 ; Char=Caster ; Reflect=True ; UseCamera=False
PlayAnimation: Char=Caster ; Anim=MP_IDLE_TO_CHANT
WaitAnimation: Char=Caster
PlayAnimation: Char=Caster ; Anim=MP_CHANT ; Loop=True
Channel: Type=Summon
PlaySound: Sound=100001 ; SoundType=SoundEffect ; Volume=0.55
SetBackgroundIntensity: Intensity=0 ; Time=10
CreateVisualEffect: Char=Everyone ; SFXModel=Data/SpecialEffects/ef091/MistFloor.sfxmodel
CreateVisualEffect: Char=Everyone ; SFXModel=Data/SpecialEffects/ef091/MistWisps.sfxmodel
PlaySound: Sound=100002 ; SoundType=SoundEffect ; Volume=0.5
Wait: Time=15

// ---- P2  THE COALESCE  (t 25 -> 40)  MANIFEST FRAME 0 STARTS HERE ---------------------------------
// NIMBRA rises out of the mist over the enemy line, from below the frame, in one second: the Movement
// piece (-900 -> +120) and the Scaling ramp (0.15 -> 1.0) both run 15 ticks and the `emerge` clip runs
// at Speed 6 over the same 15, so the unfurl, the growth and the rise are ONE gesture, as authored.
WaitSFXLoaded: SFX=91 ; Reflect=True
PlaySFX: SFX=91 ; Reflect=True ; SkipSequence=True
Wait: Time=15

// ---- P3  THE DRIFT (THE LOOK) + THE WIND-BACK  (t 40 -> 83) ---------------------------------------
// The aura dies, Iviv commits the cast gesture, and NIMBRA hangs there. Frames 15-40 (t 40-65) are the
// `driftlook` clip -- one full sway cycle, the ribbons, the 12-degree mask turn: THE LOOK, the identity
// beat the census protected at 25 ticks. Frames 40-58 (t 65-83) are the FIRST 18 ticks of `strike`: the arms
// drawing up and behind, the mask tipping down. It has not attacked. It is winding up.
// The fixed Wait is THE PHASE-LOCK RULE in force (a WaitAnimation here would slide the strike beat off
// the creature's own clip -- and this round the alignment is 18 ticks tighter than before).
StopChannel
PlayAnimation: Char=Caster ; Anim=MP_MAGIC
Wait: Time=43

// ---- P4  THE STRIKE  (t 83 -> 133) ----------------------------------------------------------------
// t=83 is the `strike` clip's LUNGE PEAK (manifest frame 58). Sting + flash + relight all fire on it:
// the light returning IS the impact. The relight ramp (18) completes at t=101; both EffectPoints then
// fire in a fully LIT window -- THE FIGURE-VISIBILITY LAW, at its exact 12-tick floor.
// 50 ticks, unchanged from the shipped build: this phase is the one the laws pin, and the retime did
// not touch it (STORYBOARD 4.3's STRUCTURAL FLOOR).
PlaySound: Sound=100003 ; SoundType=SoundEffect ; Volume=0.7
CreateVisualEffect: Char=AllTargets ; SFXModel=Data/SpecialEffects/ef091/RiftFlash.sfxmodel
SetBackgroundIntensity: Intensity=1 ; Time=18
Wait: Time=30
// t=113, manifest frame 88: the Scaling dissolve began at frame 85 (t 110), so the wisps peel off the
// creature WHILE the damage numbers pop -- the dissolve is overlapped into the damage window rather
// than queued after it. That overlap is where the shipped build's separate 75-tick P5 hold went.
CreateVisualEffect: Char=Everyone ; SFXModel=Data/SpecialEffects/ef091/MistWisps.sfxmodel
EffectPoint: Char=AllTargets ; Type=Effect
Wait: Time=12
EffectPoint: Char=Everyone ; Type=Figure
Wait: Time=8

// ---- P5  THE DISSOLVE + RELEASE  (t 133 -> 140) ---------------------------------------------------
// WaitSFXDone holds the last 2 ticks until the instance drains at t=135 (25 + the 110-tick window);
// StopSound kills the drone on that tick (the 8.0 s master has already faded out naturally at t~130,
// so this is a safety, not an audible cut); the cast closes on Anim=Idle -- THE ANIM=IDLE RELEASE LAW
// (the literal string "Idle" takes the releaseCmdIdle branch at UnifiedBattleSequencer.cs:505).
WaitSFXDone: SFX=91 ; Reflect=True
StopSound: Sound=100001 ; SoundType=SoundEffect
ActivateReflect
WaitReflect
PlayAnimation: Char=Caster ; Anim=Idle
Turn: Char=Caster ; BaseAngle=Default ; Time=5
WaitTurn: Char=Caster

// 36 operation lines (counted by summons/seqlint.py, which parses exactly as the engine does). Fixed
// waits sum to 123 ticks (15 + 15 + 43 + 30 + 12 + 8) -- down from 395. The two P0 clip-bound waits are
// budgeted at ~10 and are the only uncertainty in the cast (+-10 ticks) -- and they sit BEFORE PlaySFX,
// so that slack shifts every phase uniformly and the .seq/manifest two-clock alignment is untouched.
// Total = ~10 clip + 123 fixed + the 2 ticks WaitSFXDone blocks + the 5-tick release Turn = ~140.
//
// R15 (STORYBOARD 7.1): ef091/Sequence.seq is never written. SFXData.LoadSFX reads it unconditionally
// (SFXData.cs:174) -- a missing file is a graceful null, a PRESENT one would thread in as a second,
// duplicate-damage parallel thread. `SkipSequence=True` on PlaySFX is carried anyway, belt and braces.
